1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,730
In Ireland, TikTok Shop gives a seller
one shipping option: Ship by Seller.

2
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:08,582
There is no Fulfilled by TikTok here.

3
00:00:09,132 --> 00:00:12,672
That means every seller either
ships every order themselves,

4
00:00:12,692 --> 00:00:14,800
or hands that job to a warehouse.

5
00:00:15,350 --> 00:00:17,738
I run that warehouse, in Limerick.

6
00:00:17,938 --> 00:00:22,474
This is what happens to your stock from the
moment it arrives to the moment it leaves.

7
00:00:22,674 --> 00:00:24,412
One step at a time.

8
00:00:30,562 --> 00:00:33,097
The work starts before the van does.

9
00:00:33,647 --> 00:00:37,857
You tell us what's coming: which products,
how many of each, and roughly when.

10
00:00:38,407 --> 00:00:42,451
That one message settles half
the problems before they exist.

11
00:00:42,651 --> 00:00:45,472
We know which shelf the stock is going to.

12
00:00:45,672 --> 00:00:49,896
We know what a full delivery should
look like, so we can tell when it isn't.

13
00:00:50,096 --> 00:00:54,880
And we know which items need extra care:
glass, liquids, anything with a cap.

14
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:58,232
When the carton turns
up, nobody is guessing.

15
00:00:58,432 --> 00:01:01,672
We're checking it against
a list you already gave us.

16
00:01:07,821 --> 00:01:10,282
This is the step I care about most.

17
00:01:10,832 --> 00:01:14,449
The carton goes onto the
receiving table and gets opened.

18
00:01:14,649 --> 00:01:17,764
Everything comes out
and is laid out in rows.

19
00:01:17,964 --> 00:01:21,594
Then the whole delivery is
photographed in a single frame.

20
00:01:22,144 --> 00:01:26,037
Those photos go to you on the
day the delivery is received.

21
00:01:26,237 --> 00:01:30,374
If something arrived crushed, short,
or wrong, you see it that day.

22
00:01:30,574 --> 00:01:34,144
You find out about a problem
before your customer does.

23
00:01:34,694 --> 00:01:37,402
There's a second reason we do it this way.

24
00:01:37,602 --> 00:01:40,136
When TikTok Shop looks
into a delivery dispute,

25
00:01:40,156 --> 00:01:43,342
it asks for the item's condition
at the time it was packed,

26
00:01:43,362 --> 00:01:46,121
and for proof that it was
handed to the carrier.

27
00:01:46,321 --> 00:01:49,803
We collect exactly what's on
that list, for every order.

28
00:01:50,353 --> 00:01:53,971
Whether the platform accepts
it is the platform's decision.

29
00:01:54,171 --> 00:01:57,385
Our job is to make sure
the evidence exists.

30
00:02:03,535 --> 00:02:05,517
Three things can go wrong.

31
00:02:06,067 --> 00:02:07,821
Something is damaged.

32
00:02:08,021 --> 00:02:09,751
Something is missing.

33
00:02:09,951 --> 00:02:12,555
Or something arrived
that wasn't on the list.

34
00:02:13,105 --> 00:02:15,792
Damaged stock does not go on a shelf.

35
00:02:15,992 --> 00:02:21,146
It goes into one box, marked damaged and
on hold, so it can't be picked by mistake.

36
00:02:21,696 --> 00:02:26,272
Missing and extra items are counted
against what you told us to expect.

37
00:02:26,822 --> 00:02:31,047
Then it's your decision whether you send
it back to your supplier, write it off,

38
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:32,385
or sell it as seconds.

39
00:02:32,585 --> 00:02:35,032
Those are your decisions, not ours.

40
00:02:35,232 --> 00:02:40,044
The warehouse records the problem and
keeps the stock apart until you've decided.

41
00:02:46,194 --> 00:02:48,329
Good stock goes to the shelves.

42
00:02:48,529 --> 00:02:53,217
Every product gets a location, A1
to A6 in this bay, and a quantity.

43
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:56,458
From that point the system
says what's on the shelf,

44
00:02:56,478 --> 00:02:58,452
and the shelf has to agree with it.

45
00:02:59,002 --> 00:03:00,947
That doesn't happen by trust.

46
00:03:01,147 --> 00:03:02,921
It happens by counting.

47
00:03:03,121 --> 00:03:07,937
We recount locations and compare the number
on the shelf with the number in the record.

48
00:03:08,137 --> 00:03:12,923
If they don't match, we find out why before
it turns into an order we can't fill.

49
00:03:13,473 --> 00:03:16,776
A stock figure is only
useful if someone checked it.

50
00:03:22,926 --> 00:03:26,947
Your customer buys on TikTok
Shop or on your Shopify store.

51
00:03:27,147 --> 00:03:31,309
That order has to reach the warehouse,
with the items and the address together,

52
00:03:31,329 --> 00:03:33,067
before anything can be picked.

53
00:03:33,617 --> 00:03:36,981
However it gets to us, the
clock has already started.

54
00:03:37,181 --> 00:03:42,020
On TikTok Shop, the platform gives
a seller 48 hours to ship an order.

55
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:45,304
That's the platform's rule,
not a promise of ours.

56
00:03:45,504 --> 00:03:48,519
It's the clock every order here starts on.

57
00:03:54,669 --> 00:03:57,489
Picking goes by location, not by memory.

58
00:03:58,039 --> 00:04:00,078
The order says which product.

59
00:04:00,278 --> 00:04:02,251
The record says which shelf.

60
00:04:02,451 --> 00:04:05,847
We go to that address and
take the item from that cell.

61
00:04:06,397 --> 00:04:10,280
It sounds slower than someone who
just knows where everything is.

62
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:13,450
It isn't, and it doesn't
break when that person is off,

63
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:15,903
or when two products look almost the same.

64
00:04:16,453 --> 00:04:18,889
An address is something you can check.

65
00:04:19,089 --> 00:04:20,490
Memory isn't.

66
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:29,853
Packaging is chosen by
category, not by habit.

67
00:04:30,403 --> 00:04:33,355
A polybag for soft goods that can't break.

68
00:04:33,555 --> 00:04:37,202
A padded mailer for small things
that need some cushioning.

69
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:41,422
A box for glass, liquids and
anything with a shape to protect.

70
00:04:41,972 --> 00:04:44,436
Size matters as much as protection.

71
00:04:44,636 --> 00:04:49,396
Couriers charge by dimensional weight:
length times width times height,

72
00:04:49,416 --> 00:04:50,643
divided by 5000.

73
00:04:50,843 --> 00:04:54,846
They bill whichever is bigger,
that figure or the actual weight.

74
00:04:55,046 --> 00:04:59,698
So a light item in a box that's
too big is paid for as a heavy one.

75
00:05:00,248 --> 00:05:03,996
For cosmetics the rules are
specific: tape the cap and bag it,

76
00:05:04,016 --> 00:05:07,691
make sure glass can't move,
and keep stock away from heat.

77
00:05:07,891 --> 00:05:10,681
There's a separate video on exactly that.

78
00:05:16,831 --> 00:05:18,935
The parcel goes on the scale.

79
00:05:19,135 --> 00:05:22,014
The weight and the order
produce the shipping label,

80
00:05:22,034 --> 00:05:24,023
and the label goes on the parcel.

81
00:05:24,573 --> 00:05:29,345
Finished parcels go into the dispatch cage,
and the cage is handed to the carrier.

82
00:05:29,895 --> 00:05:34,077
The parcel leaves with a tracking number,
and that number goes onto the order,

83
00:05:34,097 --> 00:05:35,917
so your customer can follow it.

84
00:05:36,467 --> 00:05:39,566
Every carrier has a
daily collection cut-off.

85
00:05:39,766 --> 00:05:42,298
The warehouse plans the
day backwards from it,

86
00:05:42,318 --> 00:05:45,241
so the packing is finished
before the van arrives.

87
00:05:51,391 --> 00:05:53,737
A return isn't one job.

88
00:05:53,937 --> 00:05:55,050
It's five.

89
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:59,680
We receive it, inspect it, grade it,
repack it if it can be sold again,

90
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:01,409
and put it back into stock.

91
00:06:01,959 --> 00:06:06,615
That's Dockentra, in Limerick, for
brands on TikTok Shop and Shopify.

92
00:06:06,815 --> 00:06:12,590
From €2.60 per order, €0.60 per
additional item in the same order,

93
00:06:12,610 --> 00:06:16,008
a €275 monthly minimum, no setup fee.

94
00:06:16,208 --> 00:06:19,578
Every price is published at dockentra.ie.

